  {
    "text": "API Delays and Portfolio Valuation Mechanics",
    "uses": [
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 1280,
        "block": "hydrated-0001"
      },
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 1280,
        "block": "hydrated-0003"
      },
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 360,
        "block": "hydrated-0001"
      },
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 360,
        "block": "hydrated-0003"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "text": "Examine how data transmission delays, API snapshots, and cache intervals impact the valuation and execution of virtual portfolios.",
    "uses": [
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 1280,
        "block": "hydrated-0002"
      },
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 360,
        "block": "hydrated-0002"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "text": "Examine how data transmission delays, API snapshots, and cache intervals impact the valuation and execution of virtual portfolios. Observation time, fetch time and periodic sampling describe different parts of a data feed. Delayed marks can differ from a contemporaneous comparison quote, whose own venue and timestamp must be stated.",
    "uses": [
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 1280,
        "block": "hydrated-0004"
      },
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 360,
        "block": "hydrated-0004"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "text": "The Architecture of Price Delivery",
    "uses": [
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 1280,
        "block": "hydrated-0005"
      },
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 360,
        "block": "hydrated-0005"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "text": "Delivery through an API can involve timestamps, caching, rate limits and service interruptions. Update schedules differ by endpoint and plan; this lesson does not assert a universal delay for free services. Distinguish the provider observation time from the time the page fetched it. A successful HTTP response need not contain a fresh observation, and a failed request supplies no new market price. Use the actual status and timestamps before interpreting a practice valuation.",
    "uses": [
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 1280,
        "block": "hydrated-0006"
      },
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 360,
        "block": "hydrated-0006"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "text": "An observation can be older than the time it reaches a dashboard. A snapshot series can also omit price changes between observations; this is not proof that a smoothing algorithm was applied. Aggregation, sampling, caching and transmission are distinct processes with different timestamps. Their effect depends on the learning question and market conditions. Record the provider observation time and fetch time separately, and keep missing observations distinct from a zero price. A recent page refresh or successful response cannot establish that the underlying observation is fresh or executable.",
    "uses": [
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 1280,
        "block": "hydrated-0007"
      },
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 360,
        "block": "hydrated-0007"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "text": "Valuing a Virtual Portfolio",
    "uses": [
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 1280,
        "block": "hydrated-0008"
      },
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 360,
        "block": "hydrated-0008"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "text": "A marked holding value is its recorded virtual quantity multiplied by its selected valuation input. Total virtual portfolio equity includes all marked holdings and remaining cash. A delayed observation may postpone a displayed change; it does not remove exposure to falling prices. State the observation time and distinguish cached or fixed simulator inputs from contemporary market evidence.",
    "uses": [
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 1280,
        "block": "hydrated-0009"
      },
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 360,
        "block": "hydrated-0009"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "text": "A historical close or snapshot can provide a valuation reference. It does not necessarily determine the recorded practice execution price. TradeHQ labels chart and practice price inputs separately; a delayed reference does not model an actual venue fill or its liquidity costs. Keep the valuation timestamp, recorded simulation fill and fee separate when interpreting the fictional ledger.",
    "uses": [
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 1280,
        "block": "hydrated-0010"
      },
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 360,
        "block": "hydrated-0010"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "text": "Slippage and Execution Realities",
    "uses": [
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 1280,
        "block": "hydrated-0011"
      },
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 360,
        "block": "hydrated-0011"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "text": "A separate worksheet can compare hypothetical execution differences, not actual venue liquidity. TradeHQ distinguishes guest browser price inputs from signed-in server-selected eligible quotes and charges a simulated transaction fee. The estimate displayed before submission can differ from the recorded fill. Neither mode models exchange order-book priority or calibrated slippage.",
    "uses": [
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 1280,
        "block": "hydrated-0012"
      },
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 360,
        "block": "hydrated-0012"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "text": "For a hypothetical 1% adverse buy adjustment to a $10 reference, the assumed fill is $10.10. This arithmetic cannot establish that the real market had that price or enough available quantity. An actual historical fill would require a matched timestamp, venue and execution record. A separate fee remains a different cost from slippage. Label invented adjustments as assumptions and compare more than one path; changing the scenario does not make practice results a reliable forecast.",
    "uses": [
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 1280,
        "block": "hydrated-0013"
      },
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 360,
        "block": "hydrated-0013"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "text": "Practice Task: Estimating Valuation Discrepancies",
    "uses": [
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 1280,
        "block": "hydrated-0014"
      },
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 360,
        "block": "hydrated-0014"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "text": "For this exercise, assume you manage a virtual portfolio holding exactly one hundred units of an asset. The live exchange price is currently twelve dollars per unit, but your paper-trading dashboard is linked to a delayed API feed that updates every ten minutes. The current dashboard display shows a price of eleven dollars and fifty cents per unit, which was the exchange rate ten minutes ago. Calculate both the current paper valuation and the actual real-time market value of your holdings.",
    "uses": [
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 1280,
        "block": "hydrated-0015"
      },
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 360,
        "block": "hydrated-0015"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "text": "To solve this, multiply your one hundred units by the dashboard price of eleven dollars and fifty cents, yielding a paper valuation of one thousand one hundred fifty dollars. Next, calculate the live market value by multiplying your one hundred units by twelve dollars, which equals one thousand two hundred dollars. The fifty-dollar discrepancy represents the temporary valuation lag caused by the API delay. Record the discrepancy and the two observation times before interpreting this fictional valuation. The arithmetic alone does not establish how a learner will act.",
    "uses": [
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 1280,
        "block": "hydrated-0016"
      },
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 360,
        "block": "hydrated-0016"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "text": "Observation time, fetch time and periodic sampling describe different parts of a data feed.",
    "uses": [
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 1280,
        "block": "hydrated-0018"
      },
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 360,
        "block": "hydrated-0018"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "text": "Delayed marks can differ from a contemporaneous comparison quote, whose own venue and timestamp must be stated.",
    "uses": [
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 1280,
        "block": "hydrated-0019"
      },
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 360,
        "block": "hydrated-0019"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "text": "A hypothetical slippage assumption and a separately charged fee do not reproduce actual order-book execution.",
    "uses": [
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 1280,
        "block": "hydrated-0020"
      },
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 360,
        "block": "hydrated-0020"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "text": "The network bandwidth restrictions imposed by local internet providers.",
    "uses": [
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 1280,
        "block": "hydrated-0023"
      },
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 360,
        "block": "hydrated-0023"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "text": "API transmission latency and data caching intervals.",
    "uses": [
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 1280,
        "block": "hydrated-0024"
      },
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 360,
        "block": "hydrated-0024"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "text": "Manual authorization steps required for every virtual market trade.",
    "uses": [
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 1280,
        "block": "hydrated-0025"
      },
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 360,
        "block": "hydrated-0025"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "text": "Government monitoring procedures that freeze prices temporarily.",
    "uses": [
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 1280,
        "block": "hydrated-0026"
      },
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 360,
        "block": "hydrated-0026"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "text": "It prevents users from executing any buy or sell transactions.",
    "uses": [
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 1280,
        "block": "hydrated-0027"
      },
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 360,
        "block": "hydrated-0027"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "text": "It permanently locks the account balance until the live market closes.",
    "uses": [
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 1280,
        "block": "hydrated-0028"
      },
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 360,
        "block": "hydrated-0028"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "text": "It creates a temporary discrepancy between paper values and live market rates.",
    "uses": [
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 1280,
        "block": "hydrated-0029"
      },
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 360,
        "block": "hydrated-0029"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "text": "It forces the portfolio to automatically convert all assets to cash.",
    "uses": [
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 1280,
        "block": "hydrated-0030"
      },
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 360,
        "block": "hydrated-0030"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "text": "It guarantees the actual venue fill",
    "uses": [
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 1280,
        "block": "hydrated-0031"
      },
      {
        "path": "/courses/cryptocurrency-price-feeds-and-valuation/api-delays-and-portfolio-valuation",
        "width": 360,
        "block": "hydrated-0031"
      }
    ]
